From: Koji Ishii <kojii@chromium.org>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 02:27:33 -0700
Subject: [webvtt] Make text-track pseudo-elements read-only

Add `-webkit-user-modify: read-only !important` to the
`video::-webkit-media-text-track-*` rules in `mediaControls.css` so
author CSS cannot make internal WebVTT text-track elements in the user
agent shadow root editable or focusable.

Most other user agent shadow pseudo-elements in `html.css` and
`input_multiple_fields.css` already set `-webkit-user-modify: read-only
!important`.

While it is also possible to enforce this in C++, pinning the property
in the UA stylesheet is a safer and lower-risk fix for backporting.

Fixed: 574412629
Change-Id: Ibd85ec254e2d3639c6ced8891243954338f74b0d
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8610568
Reviewed-by: Kent Tamura <tkent@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Koji Ishii <kojii@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1722739}

Electron adaptation notes (44-x-y):
The media_controls_impl_test.cc changes conflicted with this branch's version
of the test and were dropped; the mediaControls.css change is applied verbatim.

